WEBVTT


00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:05.480
Watch as we knit warm, double the
ear flaps that can be added to the

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:07.610
hats in our Ear Flap Hat Collection.

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:12.469
Start with an open cast on
with waste yarn and ravel cord.

00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:19.570
Knit the straight section
according to the pattern.

00:00:23.919 --> 00:00:25.270
Set the carriage to hold.

00:00:26.729 --> 00:00:28.049
On the carriage side.

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:32.309
Start the short row decreases
by pulling needles to hold.

00:00:41.279 --> 00:00:45.630
Add weight and use your fingers to make
sure all of the stitches knit correctly.

00:00:50.115 --> 00:00:54.225
Start the short row increases
by putting needles opposite the

00:00:54.225 --> 00:00:56.595
carriage back into working position.

00:01:07.104 --> 00:01:11.845
Again, use weight and your fingers to
ensure that everything knits properly.

00:01:11.845 --> 00:01:21.525
Knit straight according to your pattern.

00:01:34.345 --> 00:01:37.945
Join the two edges by picking
up the open cast on stitches.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:53.449
Wrap the tail of yarn around the
first needle, pull out the Ravel

00:01:53.449 --> 00:01:56.430
cord and remove the scrap yarn.

00:01:57.259 --> 00:01:58.460
Knit one row.

00:01:58.699 --> 00:02:01.280
This will make it easier
to hang the flaps.

00:02:01.669 --> 00:02:05.900
You can always remove this extra
row if you decide you don't want it.

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:08.789
And scrap off.

00:02:08.789 --> 00:02:20.090
Knit the second flap and
you're ready to knit your hat.

